     1,
     "This problem seems quite complex, can you supply a fully reproducible example to help us out? <div><br></div><div>B<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Oct 30, 2012 at 1:01 PM, Mortimer Cladwell <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mbcla...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Hi,<u></u><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Using the drc package I want to overlay EC50 curves on summary stats (mean +/- sem) in a single plot.  I can get the summary plot no problem:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> ggplot() + <br>    coord_cartesian() +<br>\r\n\r\n      scale_x_log10() +<br>        scale_y_continuous() +<br>            layer(<br>                  data=d9,<br>                  mapping=aes(x=nM, y=100*avg,ymin=100*avg-100*sem, ymax= 100*avg+100*sem,colour=factor(name)), <br>\r\n\r\n                  stat=&quot;identity&quot;,<br>                  stat_params=list(),<br>                  geom=&quot;pointrange&quot;,<br>                  geom_params=list(),<br>                  position= &quot;identity&quot;                <br>\r\n\r\n                  )</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Which gives:<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"><a style=\"MARGIN-LEFT:1em;MARGIN-RIGHT:1em\" href=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s1600/fig1.bmp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s1600/fig1.bmp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374205029000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ByKRSUPl9z66bmvheNfcp\"><img border=\"0\" src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s320/fig1.bmp\" width=\"317\" height=\"320\"></a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">The overlay I can generate with the &quot;plot&quot; command:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">  windows()<br>  curve1.m &lt;- drm(100*avg ~ log10(nM+1), name, data = d9, <br>\r\n\r\n                  fct = LL.4(fixed =c( NA, 0, 100, NA), names = c(&quot;Slope&quot;, &quot;Lower Limit&quot;, &quot;Upper Limit&quot;, &quot;ED50&quot;)))<br>  <br>  plot(curve1.m, col=TRUE, lwd=2, ylab=&quot;% Survival&quot;, broken=TRUE, log=&quot;x&quot;, xlab=&quot;log10( nM + 1 )&quot;, ylim=c(0,150))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Looks like:</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"><a style=\"MARGIN-LEFT:1em;MARGIN-RIGHT:1em\" href=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-8d8X9MtpnUE/UI_M0-Q-y_I/AAAAAAAAAEI/4CF0Y-QI1rM/s1600/fig2.bmp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-8d8X9MtpnUE/UI_M0-Q-y_I/AAAAAAAAAEI/4CF0Y-QI1rM/s1600/fig2.bmp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374205029000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3YNcbWGM6jC6wzouhXO9Hz\"><img border=\"0\" src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-8d8X9MtpnUE/UI_M0-Q-y_I/AAAAAAAAAEI/4CF0Y-QI1rM/s320/fig2.bmp\" width=\"317\" height=\"320\"></a></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">If I try what I think would be reasonable to get it all in one ggplot2 plot:</span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"></span> </div>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">  ggplot() + <br>    coord_cartesian() +<br>\r\n\r\n      scale_x_log10() +<br>        scale_y_continuous() +<br>            layer(<br>                  data=d9,<br>                  mapping=aes(x=log10(nM+1), y=100*avg,ymin=100*avg-100*sem, ymax= 100*avg+100*sem,colour=factor(name)), <br>\r\n\r\n                  stat=&quot;identity&quot;,<br>                  stat_params=list(),<br>                  geom=&quot;pointrange&quot;,<br>                  geom_params=list(),<br>                  position= &quot;identity&quot;                <br>\r\n\r\n                  )+<br>                    <br>                    layer(<br>                          data=d9,<br>                          mapping=aes( x=log10(nM+1), y=100*avg  ), <br>                          stat=&quot;function&quot;,<br>\r\n\r\n                          stat_params=list(fun=drm, args=list(  formula=100*avg ~log10(nM+1),  data = d9,<br>                                                      fct = LL.4(fixed =c( NA, 0, 100, NA), names = c(&quot;Slope&quot;, &quot;Lower Limit&quot;, &quot;Upper Limit&quot;, &quot;ED50&quot;))    ))  ,<br>\r\n\r\n                          geom=&quot;line&quot;,<br>                          geom_params=list(),<br>                          position= &quot;identity&quot;                <br>                          )<br></span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>I get the error:<u></u></span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>Error in model.frame.default(formula = 100 * avg ~ log10(nM + 1), curveid = c(-3.65641728005737,  : <br>\r\n\r\n  variable lengths differ (found for &#39;(curveid)&#39;)<br><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>I have tried many modifications without success.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<u></u>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>Can anyone help?<u></u></span></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>Thanks<span><font color=\"#888888\"><u></u></font></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"><u></u>Mortimer</span></div>\r\n\r\n<u></u>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"></p>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374205029000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UUE7gAhsgGRZOEy2iDK9q\">https://github.com/hadley/