     "<br><br>On Tuesday, October 30, 2012 9:01:26 AM UTC-4, Mortimer Cladwell wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Hi,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Using the drc package I want to overlay EC50 curves on summary stats (mean +/- sem) in a single plot.  I can get the summary plot no problem:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\"> ggplot() + <br>    coord_cartesian() +<br>      scale_x_log10() +<br>        scale_y_continuous() +<br>            layer(<br>                  data=d9,<br>                  mapping=aes(x=nM, y=100*avg,ymin=100*avg-100*sem, ymax= 100*avg+100*sem,colour=factor(name)), <br>                  stat=&quot;identity&quot;,<br>                  stat_params=list(),<br>                  geom=&quot;pointrange&quot;,<br>                  geom_params=list(),<br>                  position= &quot;identity&quot;                <br>                  )</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">Which gives:</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"> </div>\r\n<div style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:center;CLEAR:both\"><a style=\"MARGIN-LEFT:1em;MARGIN-RIGHT:1em\" href=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s1600/fig1.bmp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s1600/fig1.bmp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374205032000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2juECIOUpMizYjQIuUuTTJ\"><img src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-Aw_xC-rYt8M/UI7a0pV9YPI/AAAAAAAAAD4/7NO4qqxdghM/s320/fig1.bmp\" border=\"0\" height=\"320\" width=\"317\"></a></div>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">The overlay I can generate with the &quot;plot&quot; command:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERTICAL-ALIGN:baseline\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Arial&#39;,&#39;sans-serif&#39;;COLOR:#222222;FONT-SIZE:10pt\">  windows()<br>  curve1.m &lt;- drm(100*avg ~ log10(nM+1), name, data = d9, <br>                  fct = LL.4(fixed =c( NA, 0, 100, NA), names = c(&quot;Slope&quot;, &quot;Lower Limit&quot;, &quot;Upper Limit&quot;, &quot;ED50&quot;)))<br>  <br>  plot(curve1.m, col=TRUE, lwd=2, ylab=&quot;% Survival&quot;, broken=TRUE, log=&quot;x&quot;, xlab=&quot;log10( nM + 1 )&quot;, ylim=c(0,150))</span></p>\r\n<div style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN:0in 0in 0pt;BACKGROUND:white;VERT